<title>FRANCE: French CSA opinion poll gives right seat majority.</title>
<headline>French CSA opinion poll gives right seat majority.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of an opinion poll of French voters' intentions ahead of the May 25/June 1 parliamentary election.</p>
<p>The telephone poll of 1,003 adults aged 18 and over was conducted by Louis Harris on May 5 and May 6 and made public on May 6.</p>
<p>			   Percentage	  Seat projections in</p>
<p>			    of vote	     National Assembly</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left	     1.5			0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		 10			 21</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left  30			232</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Ecologists		  4.5		    (*)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR/UDF-other right    40.5		    301</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front	   13.5			1</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>* no separate figure given for ecologists.</p>
<p>The seat projections cover the 555 constituencies in metropolitan France, not the 22 seats in overseas departments and territories.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
